Zaragoga, Spain; 2002, August 28&#x02013;31</source></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>Zoonoses Directive named European Council Directive (92/117/EEC) concerning measures for protection against specified zoonoses and specific zoonotic agents in animals and products of animal origin in order to prevent outbreaks of food-borne infections and intoxications, as amended</article-title><source>OJ of the European Communities L</source><volume>62</volume><fpage>38</fpage><lpage>48</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>European Parliament and the Council Directive (2003/99/EC) on the monitoring of zoonoses and zoonotic agents amending Council Decision 90/424/EEC and repealing Council Directive 92/117/EEC</article-title><source>OJ of the European Communities L</source><volume>325</volume><fpage>31</fpage><lpage>40</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>European Parliament and Council Regulation (2160/2003) on the control of salmonella and other specified food-borne zoonotic agents</article-title><source>OJ of the European Communities L</source><volume>325</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>15</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dorfman</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Dorfman R, Dorfman NS</surname></name></person-group><source>An introduction to benefit-cost analysis in economics of the environment &#x02013; selected readings</source><year>1993</year><publisher-name>W.W. Norton &#x00026; Company, Inc. London</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krupnick</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Valuing health benefits &#x02013; policy choises and technical issues</article-title><source>RFF Report 2004, March Washington DC</source></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ranta</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Maijala</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A probabilistic transmission model of <italic>Salmonella </italic>in the primary broiler production chain</article-title><source>Risk Anal</source><year>2002</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>47</fpage><lpage>58</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12017361</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/0272-4332.t01-1-00004</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maijala</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ranta</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><source><italic>Salmonella </italic>in broiler production in Finland &#x02013; a quantitative risk assessment</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>National Veterinary and Food Research Institute publication 04/2003, Helsinki, Finland</publisher-name><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15009340</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maijala</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ranta</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Seuna</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Pelkonen</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Johansson</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A quantitative risk assessment of the public health impact of the Finnish salmonella control program for broilers</article-title><source>Int J Food Microbiology</source><year>2005</year><volume>102</volume><fpage>21</fpage><lpage>35</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ijfoodmicro.2004.11.012</pub-i